{
  "capture": "telemetry/mg90-d__dev-v006-2A-D",
  "notes": "stage 4 current-zero of mg90-d on dev-v006-2A-D, no capture of its own: every stage 3 sweep of the pair in time order (521 sweeps, four days) through oscnb.sweeps.row_store and oscnb.zero. One servo, one board. Truth: the crest column's mean over the last 100 ms of a coast of 100 ms past its settle ticks; a drive run takes the tail nearest its first row; 244 sweeps carry one. Error: the float tracker's awake zero (64-bit state, the estimator of record; the integer Q16 port reads 0.0625 lower) less the truth, the run mean unless named. Classes: cold after 200 stale periods of rest, rail moved past half a count of stage 1's step line, else warm. Brackets: 95 % from resampling sweeps (2000 draws, seed 1); paired differences over the same runs. truth_floor: median range of a sweep's tails over sweeps with two or more. Feed: duty gate 30 %, settled coast, torque off; the trough share fits OLS at 30 % or narrower, +/- se. Unit 1's gate-width rows are float, its current-gate and share rows the integer port. Start rule: seed awake = asleep + step(rail) at boot and when the rail moves past seed_rail_threshold_v (sqrt(line held-out rms^2 - held zero sd^2) / slope, bounds the flat band) for 32 rail rows, the rail read off the driven terminal; step line held out by capture set. Hold: |difference| of two 100 ms truth readings on one rail (within 0.1 count of step), 1 s inside one coast, 10 and 60 s tail pairs; bounds of p90 by resampling the earlier sweep. Noise: settled stretches, Welch 2048 rows; low end 16384 rows on coasts of 0.8 s and more. Constant: per sweep the narrow drives' trough less its coast truth; the coast fed from the crest column; held out by day (bounds of drive_feed_offset: the four folds). Design: start rule + constant held out by day, all 975 runs, age gap model. results/<pair>.step.csv: the step by rail band with the line and curve held out by capture set; results/<pair>.alpha.csv: the zero against alpha 2^-9 to 2^-15.",
